=== subjectKindLaw ===
"What a subject-scope's `subjects` entries IDENTIFY, per relation. `source-path`: each subject is a path in the snapshot this scope names, so the scope's own extent is exactly those paths - `file` and `vcs-change` bind it through their registry snapshotJoins pathField, and `clones` binds it through bodyIdentityJoin, whose single anchor IS the body span the identity is over. `package-name`: a package identifier, not a path. `symbol`: an opaque SubjectIdV1 that the record associates with no path; the enumerator's attribution of symbols to files is trusted and is NOT re-derivable from the retained Run, so no per-subject path law is possible for these relations and any capability question about them can only be answered at the coarser retained extent. That limit is stated rather than worked around: inventing symbol-to-path parsing would be fabricated evidence."

=== coverageTotalityLaw whichRelations ===
{
  "standing": "Normative and CLOSED. A relation row carries a `coverageTotality` row only where the relation's own meaning makes its rung TOTAL over the snapshot inventory. A relation with no row declares that a subject may lawfully bear no fact, which is itself the record that nothing further constrains it.",
  "whyItIsNeeded": "`entry.coverage: complete` is a claim that the committed examined partition was examined exhaustively. For a rung that is total over the inventory that claim also decides a universal negative: over a COMPLETE `file@enumerated` Coverage, `exists file where path=P` is authoritative, so a complete result that retains no fact for an inventoried subject asserts that an inventoried file is ABSENT. On frozen v13 that graph closed - a `file@enumerated` scope over the inventoried subject `a.ts`, `coverage: complete`, `deficiency: null` and zero facts. Nothing derived the obligation, so nothing refused it.",
  "whichRelationsHaveOne": "`file@enumerated` only. A snapshot inventories exactly the files it contains, so every inventoried path has exactly one file fact and an omission is an error. `package@manifest-declared` and `vcs-change@vcs-reported` are NOT total and get no row: most paths declare no package and most paths were not changed, so their empty results are ordinary findings rather than omissions. Applying totality to them would manufacture obligations the relations do not carry.",
  "whatItDoesNotRequire": "Only subjects that are IN the snapshot inventory are owed a fact. A scope naming a path the snapshot does not contain is answered honestly by a complete result with no fact for it - the host examined the question and the file is genuinely absent. And the law is conditional on `coverage: complete`: an `unknown` result with its disclosed deficiency owes nothing, which is what keeps a partially examined inventory representable.",
  "enforcedAt": "identity-model close_run, over the RETAINED view's own facts and the retained snapshot inventory, alongside the other Coverage prerequisites. It reads no claimed value except the `complete` it is judging."
}

=== snapshotJoinLaw ===
Normative. Each row states what the enclosing fact snapshot must contain for this relation payload to be admissible. Rows are applied by identity-model close_run on every owning fact; a relation absent from this table declares that it names no snapshot path and no retained artifact, which is itself the record that nothing constrains it.

